00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:14.670
Within a country, wealth and power are almost
always concentrated in just a few small regions.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:20.470
In the U.S., 37 of the 75 highest-earning
counties lie in the Northeastern corridor

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:23.420
between Washington D.C. and Boston.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:29.290
And 54% of startups are first financed in
just five metropolitan areas.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.570
Trace the coasts and there you will find the
rich and powerful.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:35.140
China is no exception.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:39.410
The historic, political-capital of D.C. is
Beijing,

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:43.250
The bustling, financial-center of New York
is Shanghai,

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:47.880
And the fast-paced, innovative Silicon Valley
is the southern city of Shenzhen.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:54.370
Together, it, Hong Kong, Macau, Guangzhou,
and several other cities form the Pearl River

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:59.570
Delta, one of the wealthiest and most vibrant
parts of China, and one of the most important

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.980
to the world economy.

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:05.660
It’s home to the third, fifth, and seventh
busiest container ship ports.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:10.790
It’s where your iPhone came from, And where
it will eventually end up.

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:16.500
But while these are among China’s most internationally
open, connected, and capitalist cities, they’re

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:20.070
also the most disconnected domestically.

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:25.240
Despite being part of China, Hong Kong and
Macau have separate governments, laws, and

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:26.240
freedoms.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:30.770
Residents of the two Special Administrative
Regions require a permit to cross the border

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:33.100
into the mainland, and vice versa.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:39.010
Legally, they’re islands, and doing business
across them involves a sea of bureaucracy.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.920
At least, until now.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:47.450
China plans to integrate all these cities
into one Greater Bay Area - a megacity 58%

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.689
bigger than the entire Tokyo Metropolitan
Area.

00:01:50.689 --> 00:01:54.860
San Fransisco’s Bay Area is home to about
7 million people.

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:56.729
China’s, almost 70.

00:01:56.729 --> 00:02:02.630
It hopes to rival both Silicon Valley and
Wall Street - at the same time, with an economy

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:06.210
already the size of South Korea or Russia.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:10.940
But many argue there’s another, hidden motivation
behind China’s plan.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:18.800
The train from West Kowloon, in downtown Hong
Kong, to Futian Station in Shenzhen, mainland

00:02:18.809 --> 00:02:21.799
China takes just 14 minutes.

00:02:21.799 --> 00:02:26.029
But in those 26 kilometers, almost everything
changes.

00:02:26.029 --> 00:02:31.579
British electrical outlets are replaced with
the Type I used in Australia and New Zealand.

00:02:31.579 --> 00:02:36.629
Sites like YouTube, Twitter, and Facebook
stop working, thanks to the Great Firewall,

00:02:36.629 --> 00:02:39.989
The Hong Kong Dollar becomes the Chinese Yuan,

00:02:39.989 --> 00:02:44.970
and the average income drops from 46 to 30,000
U.S. Dollars.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:49.510
All of this is due to Hong Kong’s unique
and complicated history.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:56.549
On June 30th, 1997, the United Kingdom officially
withdrew from the territory after 156 years

00:02:56.549 --> 00:02:58.129
of governance.

00:02:58.129 --> 00:03:02.079
And on July 1st, Hong Kong was returned to
China.

00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:04.209
But not without compromise.

00:03:04.209 --> 00:03:08.669
The Sino-British Joint Declaration stated
that, although Hong Kong would exist under

00:03:08.669 --> 00:03:13.540
the sovereignty of China, it was guaranteed
its own constitution, capitalist and legal

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.579
systems for 50 years.

00:03:15.579 --> 00:03:19.650
"Hong Kong will be directly under the authority
of the Central People's Government of the

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:23.969
People’s Republic of China and will enjoy
a high degree of autonomy, except in foreign

00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:25.439
and defense affairs.”

00:03:25.439 --> 00:03:28.200
One country; Two systems.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:33.120
Likewise, the Portuguese and Chinese governments
signed the Joint Declaration on the Question

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.650
of Macau.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:39.430
But with separate, detached governments come
separate, detached economies.

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:45.930
For a region so dependent on trade and tourism,
traveling between cities is remarkably complicated.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:50.859
While the train from Hong Kong to Shenzhen
only takes 14 minutes, it first requires a

00:03:50.859 --> 00:03:53.599
lengthy immigration and customs process.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:59.029
First, by going through security, then, the
Hong Kong Departure procedure, and finally,

00:03:59.029 --> 00:04:03.459
receiving mainland arrival clearance, which
requires a separate visa.

00:04:03.459 --> 00:04:08.019
On the other side of Hong Kong, the longest
sea-crossing in the world connects to Macau

00:04:08.019 --> 00:04:10.219
and the mainland city of Zhuhai.

00:04:10.219 --> 00:04:15.930
But this $19 Billion dollar bridge which took
eight years to build, is surprisingly quiet.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:23.330
In 2018, 36 million people visited Macau,
88% of whom came from the mainland or Hong

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:27.120
Kong, but only about one million total entered
through the bridge.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:33.599
The crossing is an amazing feat of engineering,
but also a bureaucratic nightmare.

00:04:33.599 --> 00:04:37.650
Because all three territories have separate
laws and regulations, crossing the bridge

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:40.620
requires three separate insurance policies.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:46.419
In Hong Kong, car insurance is required to
cover $12.74 million US Dollars in damages,

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:55.930
on the mainland, a tiny $18,172 dollars, and,
in Macau, a minimum of $185,524.

00:04:55.930 --> 00:05:01.419
Such a huge difference makes creating a single,
unified policy extremely difficult.

00:05:01.419 --> 00:05:06.169
And because of their British and Portuguese
influence, Hong Kong and Macau drive on the

00:05:06.169 --> 00:05:07.990
left side of the road.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:12.669
But the main bridge section is located in
mainland waters, so Hong Kong drivers have

00:05:12.669 --> 00:05:17.080
to switch to the right-hand side as they enter
the link bridge, even though that’s still

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:22.040
in Hong Kong territory, travel briefly in
an undersea tunnel, allowing ships to pass

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:26.550
overhead, and then change back to the left
side if they enter Macau.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:31.629
Making things even more complicated, there’s
a quota on private cars, of course, immigration

00:05:31.629 --> 00:05:37.560
and customs, and a toll, which, if you pay
in cash, has to be Chinese Yuan.

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:41.639
Imagine how much harder it would be work in
San Fransisco if crossing the Golden Gate

00:05:41.639 --> 00:05:47.090
required a visa, permit, changing sides of
the road twice, and a few insurance policies.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:50.689
Oh - and don’t forget to pay with Mexican
Pesos.

00:05:50.689 --> 00:05:55.410
These inefficiencies are especially pronounced
in an area so rich with startups and large

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.900
consumer markets.

00:05:56.900 --> 00:06:02.000
Doctors, lawyers, and investors, for example,
are often blocked from doing business across

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:08.930
borders despite the huge economic potential,
if not legally, then out of confusion or frustration.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:13.750
Hong Kong and San Francisco have some of the
world’s most expensive rent.

00:06:13.750 --> 00:06:19.419
The former, however, is surrounded by other
terribly expensive cities - Palo Alto, San

00:06:19.419 --> 00:06:21.919
Jose, Berkeley, and so on.

00:06:21.919 --> 00:06:26.949
Hong Kong, on the other hand, has lots of
cheap labor for China’s increasingly service-based

00:06:26.949 --> 00:06:30.659
economy, right across the border, waiting
to be tapped into.

00:06:30.659 --> 00:06:34.500
The Chinese government sees this as a major
opportunity.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:39.969
The Greater Bay Area Plan, first announced
in 2016, and just released in February, is

00:06:39.969 --> 00:06:45.509
not one, but a series of steps to connect
these cities and make use of their vast differences.

00:06:45.509 --> 00:06:50.490
Macau will continue to be the Las Vegas of
the East, thanks to its geographically central

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:53.139
location and relaxed gambling laws.

00:06:53.139 --> 00:06:59.199
Hong Kong, a global intermediary, allowing
foreign firms to invest in China, and, increasingly,

00:06:59.199 --> 00:07:02.210
for Chinese companies to access the wider
world.

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:06.150
Its airport, one of the busiest in the world,
and now in the process of building a third

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:09.790
runway, will act as a gateway to the rest
of the region.

00:07:09.790 --> 00:07:15.770
Already, 14 of its 75 million passengers a
year end up traveling to nearby cities and

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:20.710
Cathay Pacific is considering selling two-in-one
plane tickets which include train or ferry

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:23.279
travel to and from the airport.

00:07:23.279 --> 00:07:28.300
Shenzhen, meanwhile, will serve as China’s
Silicon Valley, home to some of the country’s

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:32.550
biggest companies, including DJI, Tencent,
and BYD.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:37.659
Finally, Guangzhou, as the capital of the
entire Guangdong province, is the administrative

00:07:37.659 --> 00:07:39.490
and political center.

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:44.090
And connecting them all are the first parts
of the plan: The train from Hong Kong to the

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:49.840
mainland, The Hong Kong-Macau-Zhuhai Bridge,
whose details will hopefully be worked out,

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:53.960
And another, currently in construction, will
connect Shenzhen to the other side of the

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:54.960
mainland.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:59.659
Now, as these cities become more linked together,
wealth will spread outward.

00:07:59.659 --> 00:08:04.639
The Hong Kong University of Science and Technology
has announced a second campus on the mainland,

00:08:04.639 --> 00:08:09.479
and many companies are investing in property
across the border in anticipation of the plan.

00:08:09.479 --> 00:08:14.770
Already, Shenzhen is nowhere near the cheap
source of labor it once was, and some cities

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:17.500
will likely benefit more than others.

00:08:17.500 --> 00:08:23.279
But with 70 million people, there will long
be plenty of workers in surrounding areas.

00:08:23.279 --> 00:08:28.009
The economic case for the plan, is, therefore,
hard to refute.

00:08:28.009 --> 00:08:31.300
But so is the concerning trend that has followed:

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:35.729
Remember that before you can get on the train
from Hong Kong to Shenzhen, you first have

00:08:35.729 --> 00:08:38.250
to pass mainland immigration.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:42.599
That means a portion of the terminal, in the
middle of downtown Hong Kong, is controlled

00:08:42.599 --> 00:08:46.310
by mainland authorities and governed by mainland
laws.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:52.100
Now, as an isolated event, this would be easy
to dismiss as a mere convenience for faster

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:53.100
travel.

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:56.680
After all, it’s quite similar to how the
Chinese government leases part of its Shenzhen

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:58.490
port to Hong Kong.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:01.449
But this is occurring against a much larger
backdrop.

00:09:01.449 --> 00:09:07.260
In 2014, the Chinese government changed Hong
Kong’s election rules, limiting the democratic

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:12.500
power of its people to elect their Chief Executive,
to which Hong Kongers took to the streets

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:14.660
with their iconic yellow umbrellas.

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:20.120
Later, during a football match, Hong Kong
fans booed at China’s national anthem.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:26.050
It ended in a tense 0-to-0 with Chinese police
wearing riot gear warning the crowd not to

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:27.560
insult the song.

00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:31.810
The People’s Republic then passed a law
which made doing so illegal.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:36.241
And although Hong Kong is entitled to its
own laws, there’s an exception: a special

00:09:36.241 --> 00:09:41.660
section of its constitution which China has
the power to add to or remove from.

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:45.880
More recently, the Hong Kong government is
proposing changing its extradition laws to

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:49.820
allow some suspected criminals to be sent
to the mainland for prosecution.

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:55.529
Both the UK and U.S. governments have warned
that “Hong Kong’s autonomy is at risk”,

00:09:55.529 --> 00:10:01.260
but it’s also clear the world is woefully
unprepared for a China which builds not walls,

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:02.260
but bridges.

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:07.100
It’s unlikely that either country would
risk raising tensions any further.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:13.220
Meanwhile, political unity and economic growth
are China’s absolute highest priorities.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:17.959
It will argue that the redundancies of Hong
Kong and Macau’s separation loses everyone

00:10:17.959 --> 00:10:19.600
time and money.

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:24.339
Many locals, in turn, will argue that those
separations are exactly what makes their home

00:10:24.339 --> 00:10:25.910
so great.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:31.100
China will argue that no part of the Greater
Bay Area Plan fundamentally changes its relationship

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:34.860
with the regions - that protestors are overreacting.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:40.670
And skeptics will argue gradual, symbolic
changes are exactly how freedom is usually

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:42.040
lost.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:47.500
Hong Kong is unlike any other place on earth
- a culture within a culture, set to expire

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:51.459
in 2047 when its promised autonomy ends.

00:10:51.459 --> 00:10:55.310
But the new era has, in many ways, already
begun.

00:10:56.829 --> 00:11:02.889
There are about 179,000 Hong Kongers worth
a million US dollars, which, divided by its

00:11:02.889 --> 00:11:08.180
427 square miles, means you’d only need
to walk an average of 4 meters to cross paths

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.550
with a millionaire.

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:13.970
But as the world moves towards an automation-based
economy, the Greater Bay Area will need to

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:16.890
invest in high skill workers to maintain its
advantage.

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:21.421
And, truthfully, we should all be learning
skills to survive in the new economy, and

